From 15bba79f9f962e4037487961f526d5fe05ae131b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: luoxiaoyu <137460387@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:41:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MateBook X Pro 2023: Huawei profile, A7A0/WhateverXe
 evidence, AX211 installer classification

The generic builder already selects WhateverXe, itlwm, UTBDefault/USBToolBox, VoodooI2C/PS2 and
MacBookPro16,2 for this machine; this adds the Huawei-specific interpretation and closes three
evidence gaps, without changing a generic rule:

- p1401/huawei.py: board+CPU match (MRGFG-XX + i7-1360P) and notes that keep the I2C touchpad
  (GXTP786) apart from the I2C touchscreen (GXTP738X), name A7A0 in WhateverXe's table, explain
  AX211/itlwm+HeliPort, and mark the TBU405Pro USB enclosure as external, not the target.
- machine_recipes.json: Huawei recipe with ProvideCurrentCpuInfo and the 128-logical-processor
  CPUID fix used for the same i7-1360P on the XPS 9320. Status is theory: not yet booted here.
- netsupport: the installer-network decision now receives the selected kexts. itlwm is a working
  post-install driver but needs HeliPort, so AX211 is no longer counted as installer Wi-Fi; the
  build recommends Ethernet or a full offline installer.
- utbmap.map_status(): the build now says whether it used a supplied UTBMap or the generic
  UTBDefault (the no-map case this project was asked to re-check).
- intel_gpu notice matches the EFI: WhateverXe is included, the full graphics package is opt-in.
- Tests: Huawei profile, UTBMap status, AX211 installer classification, recipe.
